// CROWN modal (§11 6.3's crucible sweep): the SUBTRACT half at the
// INSTANCE altitude — an instance-unpinned handler absorbs a pinned
// instance's perform. work's row is Sample(48000); h declares no
// instance, so it is the "explicit handler bridge" SYNTAX §Parameterized
// names — the family handler serving any instance — and the install's
// subtraction clears the row, satisfying the enclosing instance-precise
// !Sample(48000). No surface exists to pin a handler to one instance,
// so over-absorption (a 44100 handler eating a 48000 perform) is
// unconstructible today; if that surface ever lands, its precision
// crucible lands with it. Expect NO E_EffectMismatch.
effect Sample(rate: Int) { tick() -> Int }
handler h { tick() => resume(1) }
fn work() with Sample(48000) = tick()
fn f() with !Sample(48000) = (work()) ~> h
fn main() = 0
